// Whether a function's runner has to look at the exit status before each block:
// only a function that may exit does (front/diag/noret/mxall.id lists them, the
// functions that call exit or abort, a noreturn function, or a function that
// calls one, and every function that calls through a pointer). Nothing else can
// make the status change while the function runs, so the load is left out.
run_chk(string name) {
  int chk = 1;
  if(find_str((import mxnames), name) < 0) {
    chk = 0;
  }
} return int chk;
given noret_init ("f"):(0)
given noret_init given noret_add("f") ("f"):(1)

// The condition of the runner's loop.
run_cond(int chk) {
  string cond = "pc >= 0";
  if(chk == 1) {
    cond = "pc >= 0 && peek64((import rtxc)) == 0";
  }
} return string cond;
(0):("pc >= 0")
(1):("pc >= 0 && peek64((import rtxc)) == 0")
